{
  "notes": [
    "12 animation ticks/sec = original 60 Hz timer divided by base_speed 5. UI refresh does not change animation speed.",
    "All dx, startX, untilX, potionX and sprite anchorX values use original DOS movement units. 1 unit = 16/7 native screen pixels.",
        "Sprites are mapped by the original frame table, not by frame+400. The complete reference table matches the reference DOS v1.4 executable byte-for-byte.",
    "Each frame dx is applied once BEFORE showing that frame. ticks controls pose duration without repeating movement.",
    "exitDx runs in the old direction BEFORE exitFlip. The run-turn handoff enters run at index 6 (frame 13).",
    "untilX triggers after the current pose duration. exitOnFrames can delay braking until a legal original pose (7 or 11).",
    "pixelAspectY 1.2 approximates DOS CRT 4:3 pixels. Use 1.0 for square source pixels.",
    "Repeated scenario steps determine pauses; all sprite timing, movement, anchors and scenario routes are editable here.",
    "The greeting retains the original Princess reunion positions, poses and 10 Hz cutscene clock (60/6). Actors share their scenario clock.",
    "The left-entry greeting mirrors the original greeting's coordinates and facing, reusing the same clips and existing sprite images through the final embrace.",
    "Princess cutscene frames 20-33 use config IDs 1020-1033. hidePrimaryActor at 1028 replaces the separate Prince with the original combined reunion sprite.",
    "The large red potion uses original dungeon body resource 163 plus red bubbles 166-172. potionGraphics offsets are native pixels; Y offsets set the exclusive sprite bottom relative to floorY+1.",
    "potionGraphics.alignWithFeet shifts the bottle and bubbles together so the bottle rests at the Prince's feet. Disable it to restore the original DOS Y offsets without changing them.",
    "Potion bubbles share the scenario tick clock. ticksPerFrame controls their animation; initialBubbleFrame fixes the original randomized starting phase for reproducible playback.",
    "Running entrances begin in the running loop fully outside the room. Phase-congruent starts retain the original braking positions and legal exit poses.",
    "startDelayTicks holds the Prince offscreen and supporting actors in their initial poses before the entrance. Potion bubbles animate on the elapsed scenario clock during the hold; actor scripts begin together afterward.",
    "Potion scenes have a 24-tick lead at 12 Hz and greeting scenes a 20-tick lead at 10 Hz, showing the potion or Princess for two seconds before the Prince starts running.",
    "The Princess waits 10 ticks for the offscreen running entrance, preserving the original contact alignment and combined-sprite handoff.",
    "The quick potion variants brake with all eight shortStop poses 53,54,55,56,49,50,51,52, retaining all 9 root movement units. shortStand holds standing pose 15 for one tick before the unchanged drink clip.",
    "After drinking, shortRecover holds standing pose 15 for one tick. shortStandingTurn then uses poses 45-51, omitting settling pose 52 and retaining the original flip and 7-unit translation; acceleration follows immediately without a standing pause.",
    "Quick potion pickup roots remain X 44 with potionX 46 facing left, and the mirrored X 96 with potionX 94 facing right. Original odd-pixel alignment and integer truncation are retained.",
    "The careful-step routes use original normal-step poses 121-132, advancing 11 DOS movement units at 12 Hz, then hold standing pose 15 for 48 ticks (four seconds). All required images already exist in the Prince asset set.",
    "carefulStepBack rewinds those poses and their positions without turning. Its pre-frame dx values undo the next forward pose's entry movement, rather than merely reversing and negating the forward list; this rewind is demo choreography.",
    "desktopEdgeEntry marks finite routes without untilX targets. The desktop renderer translates these routes to their incoming monitor edge without adding running cycles or changing their scripted travel distance."
  ],
